    content = ["# Linear Feedback Controller Parameters\n\nDefault Config\n```yaml\nlinear_feedback_controller:\n  ros__parameters:\n    <moving_joint_names>:\n      d: ''\n      p: ''\n    chainable_controller:\n      command_interfaces: ''\n      reference_prefix: ''\n    joint_velocity_filter_coefficient: 0.9\n    moving_joint_names: ''\n    pd_to_lf_transition_duration: ''\n    remove_gravity_compensation_effort: ''\n    robot_has_free_flyer: ''\n\n```\n\n## chainable_controller.command_interfaces\n\nNames of the downstream controller that takes the robot state as references.\n\n\n* Type: `string_array`\n\n\n## chainable_controller.reference_prefix\n\nNames of the downstream controller that takes the robot state as references.\n\n\n* Type: `string`\n\n* Default Value: \"\"\n\n## remove_gravity_compensation_effort\n\nDo we need to remove the gravity compensation effort? In practice some robot (like the Panda robot) drivers take as input effort and sum them with the gravity compensation effort. So we need to remove this component to our computed effort in our controller.\n\n\n* Type: `bool`\n\n\n## joint_velocity_filter_coefficient\n\nSpecifies the filter coefficient for the sensor's exponential filter. If equal to 1 the filter is inactive. I equal to zero the filter crash the signal into a constant being the initial value of the signal.\n\n\n* Type: `double`\n\n* Default Value: 0.9\n\n*Constraints:*\n - parameter must be within bounds [0.0, 1.0]\n\n*Additional Constraints:*\n\n\n\n## moving_joint_names\n\nlist of active joint names used by the controller.\n\n\n* Type: `string_array`\n\n\n*Constraints:*\n - parameter is not empty\n\n*Additional Constraints:*\n\n\n\n## robot_has_free_flyer\n\nHas the robot a freeflyer or not?\n\n\n* Type: `bool`\n\n\n## pd_to_lf_transition_duration\n\nDuration **in seconds** of transition between the PD and the LF controllers.\n\n\n* Type: `double`\n\n\n*Constraints:*\n - greater than or equal to 0.0\n\n*Additional Constraints:*\n\n\n\n## <moving_joint_names>.p\n\nProportional gains for the PD controller.\n\n\n* Type: `double`\n\n\n*Constraints:*\n - greater than or equal to 0.0\n\n*Additional Constraints:*\n\n\n\n## <moving_joint_names>.d\n\nDerivation gains for the PD controller.\n\n\n* Type: `double`\n\n\n*Constraints:*\n - greater than or equal to 0.0\n\n*Additional Constraints:*\n\n\n"],
